    "title": "2. Mid-course Reflection: What the Evidence Changed (10%)",
    "name": "Mid-course Reflection: What the Evidence Changed",
    "summary": "Reread at least three journal entries and one item from class. Identify one pattern in how you plan, monitor, respond to difficulty, or seek help. Use one course source to interpret the pattern and plan one small trial for the second half of the course.",
    "html": "<p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Worth 10% of your final course grade. Maximum score: 10 points.</p><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>PSY355, Fall 2026. Weight: 10 percent.</strong></p><h3>Your task</h3><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Reread at least three journal entries and one item from class. Identify one pattern in how you plan, monitor, respond to difficulty, or seek help. Use one course source to interpret the pattern and plan one small trial for the second half of the course.</p><h3>Format</h3><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Choose 600 to 800 words or a 4 to 5 minute audio reflection. Point to the dates of the evidence you use. A polished life story is not required; a clear explanation based on your course evidence is.</p><h3>How your work will be graded</h3><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Strong means 85 to 100 percent of a criterion, Clear means 70 to 84 percent, Developing means 50 to 69 percent, and Limited means 0 to 49 percent.</p><h3>Reading your own evidence: 3 points</h3><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:28px;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Strong:</strong> Three journal entries and an item from class reveal a precise pattern.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Clear:</strong> Required evidence supports a clear pattern.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Developing:</strong> Evidence is thin or the pattern is broad.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Limited:</strong> The reflection lacks course evidence with clear dates.</li></ul><h3>Course evidence: 3 points</h3><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:28px;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Strong:</strong> A course source is used accurately to interpret, not merely label, the pattern.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Clear:</strong> The source supports the interpretation.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Developing:</strong> Source use is partial or mostly summary.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Limited:</strong> Course evidence is absent or substantially inaccurate.</li></ul><h3>Second-half strategy trial: 2.5 points</h3><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:28px;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Strong:</strong> The next experiment is specific, realistic, and follows from the evidence.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Clear:</strong> The plan is clear and relevant.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Developing:</strong> The plan is vague or only partly connected.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Limited:</strong> No usable second-half plan is provided.</li></ul><h3>Communication: 1.5 points</h3><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:28px;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Strong:</strong> The reflection is focused, coherent, and bounded.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Clear:</strong> Communication is clear overall.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Developing:</strong> Communication is uneven.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Limited:</strong> The work is difficult to follow.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Your grade is based on the evidence in your work. Personal disclosure, polished production, and technical effects do not replace course learning.</p><h3>How to submit in Blackboard</h3><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:28px;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Open this assignment and select <strong>Start attempt</strong>. Write or paste your written work into the <strong>Submission</strong> editor using the headings in these instructions. A Word upload is optional.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Insert your required visual into the editor with a text description, or attach it as an accessible file. If you choose an audio or video format, attach the recording and captions or a transcript. A working Seneca OneDrive or Microsoft Stream link is also acceptable.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Keep all required parts together in this assignment. Before submitting, check that your text, attachments, and links open correctly.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Select <strong>Submit</strong>, wait for Blackboard’s confirmation, and keep the receipt. If you save a draft instead, return to submit it before the deadline.</li></ul><h3>Your work and permitted tools</h3><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Use your own observations, choices, explanations, and sources. Do not use generative AI to write or rewrite your submission, invent experiences or evidence, or create narration in your place. You may use spelling, dictation, screen-reader, captioning, and accessibility tools that do not generate the course content. Ask me before using a tool if you are unsure.</p><h3>Release and due dates</h3><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Released:</strong> October 19, 2026 at 12:01 a.m. Eastern.</p><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Due:</strong> October 23, 2026 at 11:59 p.m. Eastern.</p>",
